The discussion focused on the potential economic benefits of nature-based solutions (NbS) in Brazil, particularly within the context of the São Paulo Cantareira water supply system. User prompts included a request for a paragraph aimed at Ministries of Finance highlighting the economic viability of NbS. Key information shared indicated that strategic NbS investments could prevent significant drought-related losses, with quantitative results showing BRL 443.9 million in avoided losses during the 2014–2015 drought, equating to a 28% reduction in economic costs. Additionally, the analysis presented a positive net present value (NPV) of BRL 632 million from these interventions, underscoring their role in promoting long-term economic sustainability and resilience against climatic disruptions.
